cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MatrixLang: a dimension-aware optimizing compiler"
message: "Please cite the software and its technical manuscript; the manuscript is a draft for author review."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aswanth Raj"
    given-names: "A"
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science and Engineering, VIT Vellore"
  - family-names: "RANJITHKUMAR"
    given-names: "S"
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science and Engineering, VIT Vellore"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aswanth-07/matrixlang"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A compiler for a small matrix language whose types carry matrix shapes.
  Because every shape is known at compile time, the compiler can compute the
  arithmetic cost of a program before running it and choose the bracketing of a
  matrix product chain. The repository carries the compiler, a program
  generator, a five-profile eight-configuration cost study, explicit strict and
  algebraic numerical contracts, independent chain checks, a technical manuscript,
  teaching exercises, and a web demonstration. No classroom effectiveness or
  runtime speedup is claimed.
keywords:
  - compiler construction
  - computing education
  - domain-specific languages
  - type systems
  - code optimization
